NEARS-2253 — owner-accepted risk, verified AS RULED. This is NOT a defect and NOT a clean pass.

RULING 1: phone is NOT revealed to the vendor.  CONFIRMED ABSENT.
  Live GET /api/v1/vendor/order?order_id=163: 'phone' not in the delivery_man node.
  Pre/post diff records it under REMOVED — the vendor USED to receive it and no longer does.
  Pinned by test_vendor_get_order_delivery_man_is_projected_to_the_allow_list.

RULING 2: lat / lng / location / available ARE present, deliberately.  CONFIRMED PRESENT.
  Live values on order 163: lat non-null (str), lng non-null (str), location non-null (str),
  available non-null (int).

  Recording the risk precisely, because the measurement sharpens what was accepted:
  these four keys are NET-NEW to this endpoint. Pre-fix the vendor received the raw
  DeliveryMan model, which does NOT carry them — they are computed by
  deliverymen_data_formatting. The pre/post key-path diff shows them under ADDED, not
  retained. So the fix removes 23 PII keys and introduces 6, four of which constitute the
  courier live-location channel the security reviewer raised as High.

  The reviewer's mechanism is confirmed in the tree and on the wire:
    DeliveryMan::last_location() (app/Models/DeliveryMan.php:146-149) =
      hasOne(DeliveryHistory::class, 'delivery_man_id')->latestOfMany()
    — keyed on delivery_man_id, NOT order_id. It is the courier's CURRENT position,
      not their position on this order.
    VendorController::get_order applies no order_status filter. Order 163 is
      order_status='delivered' and still returned HTTP 200 with non-null lat/lng/location.
    Net effect: a store owner can poll a long-since-delivered order id indefinitely and
      read where that courier is right now.

  The owner was shown that finding in full at the approval gate and chose SHIP AS BUILT.
  QA therefore records it as an ACCEPTED RISK. It is not filed as a bug and does not
  affect the verdict. If the ruling is ever revisited, the seam is the 
  parameter on Helpers::project_order_delivery_man (currently no caller passes true).
